      "benefit": "TPD",
      "years": [2017, 2021],
      "pattern": "drift",
      "direction": "increase",
      "magnitude": "A/E rose from ~0.96 to a peak of 1.186 (+18.6%), then reverted to ~0.95-0.97 in 2022-2024",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "evidence": [
        "ae_tpd_by_year.csv: sustained YoY increase from 0.957 (2017) to 1.186 (2021)",
        "2021 deviation is ~5.5 sigma above 1.0 under Poisson null (E=897), confirming statistical significance",
        "Sharp reversion to baseline in 2022-2024 aligns with the definition of a reversionary drift; overdispersion in the full series is structural, not random volatility"
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Investigate TPD claim drivers for 2017-2021 (e.g., underwriting guideline changes, claim reporting lags, policy mix shifts, or external macro factors). Assess whether the reversion indicates a temporary experience fluctuation or a structural change requiring pricing/valuation assumption updates. Monitor subsequent years for stability."
    }
  ]
}

